// CROWN — a branch join of two named functions. `pick` returns a function that
// may perform E, so calling it performs E and `bad`'s `!E` must refuse. Boot
// equated the two rows, refused `pick` falsely and published it pure, so
// `bad` read pure. Expect E_EffectMismatch (at `bad`; see the sound dual).
effect E { op(n: Int) -> Int }
fn quiet(n) = n
fn loud(n) = op(n)
fn pick(c) = if c { quiet } else { loud }
fn bad(c) with !E = pick(c)(1)
fn main() = 0
